Have you ever noticed that some characters start out stridently aligned,
and others nominally aligned?  I thought the Neutrals started nominally
aligned, and others stridently aligned, but I checked it out in debug
mode, and this turn out not to be the case.

These are the initial alignments I found in debug mode:

 - Acheologists start out with alignment 10 (Lawful)
 - Barbarians start out with alignment 10 (Chaotic)
 - Elves start out with alignemnt 10 (Lawful)
 - Healers start out with alignment 10 (Lawful)
 - Knight start out with alignment 10 (Lawful)
 - Rogues start out with alignement 10 (Chaotic)
 - Samurais start out with alignment 10 (Lawful)


 - Cavemen start out with alignment 0 (Lawful)
 - Priests start out with alignment 0 (Neutral)
 - Tourists start out with alignment 0 (Neutral)
 - Valarkies start out with alignment 0 (Chaotic)
 - Wizards start out with alignment 0 (Neutral)

Are they really supposed to be this way?  Why doesn't everyone start
out stridently aligned?

